qs.append({"q":"The 'drain theory', put forward by early nationalists like Dadabhai Naoroji, R.C. Dutt and Dinshaw Wacha, sought to explain:","o":["British economic exploitation of India through the transformation of a self-sufficient economy into a colonial supplier of raw materials and market for British goods","The migration of Indian labour to British colonies","The decline of Mughal political authority","The causes of the 1857 Revolt"],"a":0,"e":"The drain theory analysed how British rule converted India's self-sufficient economy into a colonial one — exporting raw materials, importing finished goods, and serving as a field for British capital investment — draining India's wealth."})

